{
  "set": "real-engine-memory-first-v2",
  "description": "Pattern: the memory layer is settled before the engine answers (EGDESK_TURN_MEMORY_WRITE_FIRST=on): at the start of the turn the write judgment runs, a pending reading is stored, the pair (record, message) is judged for a conflict, and the engine is handed the settled state, so its words follow the record. write-v3's own-confirm without the flag is the baseline. Expectations by code: the store, the product's receipt (settled, conflict), words the answer must not contain. Needs --decisions, --person-home and --persisted-with-cleanup (the opt-in of the confirmation). v2 (c39): a statement that is a new record is decided at the start and stored when the turn is accepted (newrecord-first), and two unlinked records of the picked set that disagree are stated to the engine as contradicting (contradiction-first against contradiction-off; contradiction-control has nothing to mark). Expectation keys: recording.newPages, settled, contradictions; the answer of contradiction-first must name both days.",
